                <pb facs="0869" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2715: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Drew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-09T15:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. Your 108, October 5, 8 p.m. You are authorized to include in the proposed
                    exchange of notes a provision along the lines of paragraph 2 of your telegram
                    No. 106 of September 28, noon.</p>
                <p>Was the exchange of notes authorized in the Department’s telegram No. 26 of April
                    3 [<hi rendition="#italic">13</hi>], 1 p.m. effected?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
